  "scope": "Snowbank route boundaries, initial placement, priority and kerb pull-outs; weather allowance for city snow. Phase 1 remains incomplete.",
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "finding": "s1-3 and s1-10 start inside narrowings whose entry lies behind the truncated route. alongRoute returned null, hiding the narrowing and its detour; lane-centre spawns were beside pushed parked cars, rejecting even stopped candidates as collisions.",
      "evidence": "At t=0 through t=12: speed 0, hold, all 10 candidates rejected as collision, snowbank=null. Untouched s1-3 reproduced the supplied before result field-for-field except timings.",
      "fix": "Retain narrowing ends outside partial routes; place spawns and resets in the same corridor used by the driving policy."
    },
    {
      "finding": "Waiting pull-outs were counted as already inside the narrowing from their longitudinal position, although still at the kerb. Pull-outs did not check the narrowing turn before merging. A latched turn also outranked newly visible inside traffic while the approaching driver could still stop.",
      "evidence": "Probe after the boundary fix: on s1-6 car_p3 appeared at t=65.7 with ego gap 5.5 m and speed 2.24 m/s; car_p7 appeared waiting at the kerb at t=162.3. Both produced oncoming_inside conflicts. The later queue disappeared after requiring pull-outs to wait for the corridor.",
      "fix": "Exclude waiting kerb pull-outs from occupancy claims; check the shared policy before pulling out; yield a latched approach to newly visible inside traffic when stopping remains possible. auditSnowbanks and safety thresholds are unchanged."
    },
    {
      "finding": "Traffic already shifted left round a pothole could have sbShift=0 because it was already clear of snowbank-pushed parked cars. A secondary leader check omitted the pothole move and checked the unshifted lane too, falsely treating a kerb car as a leader.",
      "evidence": "After the first fixes s1-8 remained stopped through 609.7 s behind car_24 (phShift=-0.52, sbShift=0), and s1-12 was held by car_39 (phShift=-0.48, sbShift=0). The focused regression failed before the fix; after it s1-8 arrived at 368.5 s with no collision or deadlock.",
      "fix": "While snowbank policy is active, use the combined corridor offset for the secondary leader check. Keep all clearance margins and actual-obstacle checks; the regression also verifies stopping for a car genuinely in the corridor."
    },
    {
      "finding": "Some drives progress safely beyond the old snow deadline.",
      "evidence": "In the initial fixed-world probe s1-2 arrives at 293.1 s versus its old 264.8 s deadline; s1-3 arrives at 282.3 s versus 208 s, with zero deadlocks. Low-speed snowbank approaches and weather/hidden-hazard speed caps remain enforced.",
      "fix": "Only city snow deadlines are divided by WEATHER.snow.speed (0.62). Bare deadlines in every weather and city dry/rain/fog deadlines are unchanged. Persistent traffic queues still time out."
    }
  ],
